# =============================================================================
# .gitignore â€” landslide susceptibility & decision intelligence
# =============================================================================
# Principle: the repository holds code, configuration and documentation. Data
# and generated artefacts are reproducible from those three, so they are not
# tracked. The previous version committed model binaries and training
# artefacts, which is how it ended up with duplicate model files whose
# provenance nobody could reconstruct.

# --- machine-specific configuration ------------------------------------------
# Holds this machine's data_root. Never commit it; config.local.yaml.example
# documents the format instead.
config/config.local.yaml

# --- data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The delivered data assets are large (a single conditioning-factor raster is
# ~83 MB; the GLiM lithology geodatabase is >1 GB) and are validated inputs
# managed outside this repository.
/data/
*.tif
*.tiff
*.vrt
*.img
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.sbn
*.sbx
*.gdb/
*.gpkg

# --- generated artefacts ------------------------------------------------------
outputs/
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Model bundles and their attached preprocessing.
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.cbm
*.ubj
*.onnx

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# --- environments -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.conda/

# --- testing & type checking ---------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/

# --- notebooks ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Checkpoints only. Notebooks themselves are tracked, but they are exploration
# artefacts and are never part of the pipeline.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/*

# --- simulator frontend -------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output are reproducible from package-lock.json.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- editors & OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
